      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:66:2",
      "text": [
        " إِذَا كَانَ سَمْكُ الْبَيْتِ فَوْقَ سَبْعَةِ أَذْرُعٍ أَوْ قَالَ ثَمَانِيَةِ أَذْرُعٍ فَكَانَ مَا فَوْقَ السَّبْعِ وَ الثَّمَانِ الْأَذْرُعِ مُحْتَضَراً وَ قَالَ بَعْضُهُمْ مَسْكُوناً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hisham Bin Al Hakam, and someone else, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘When the ceiling of the room is above seven cubits’, or said: ‘eight cubits, what is above the seven and the eight cubits is a meeting place’, and some of them said, ‘He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘A dwelling (for Satan<sup>la</sup>)’’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hisham ibn al-Hakam and others who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If the roof of a house is higher than seven’ or as he (the Imam) said, ‘eight yards (arm-length), it is the residence of Satan or his living quarter.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
